PART 11. Five rules when building through AI
These are extremely important.

Rule 1: Never tell AI to build the entire application at once.

Build individual modules and test them.

Rule 2: Always ask AI to inspect your existing code before modifying it.

Otherwise, it might remove existing functionality or create duplicate screens.

Rule 3: Always connect your screens to real backend functionality.

A button that looks good but doesn't work isn't a completed feature.

Rule 4: Maintain a project document.

Ask your AI to maintain:
- Completed features.
- Incomplete features.
- Database structure.
- API structure.
- Known errors.
- Remaining tasks.
Rule 5: Always test before moving to the next module.

Don't let small errors accumulate until the application becomes difficult to repair.
